
### 6. Build the functions

Terraform zips the `dist` directory of `apps/api`, `apps/cron` and `apps/worker` (the zips go to `.build/`, which git ignores), so build them first:

```bash
{{runScript "build"}}
```

### 7. Deploy the dev environment

```bash
terraform -chdir=infra apply -var="env=dev"
```

`apply` shows the plan and waits for `yes`. For prod, switch the backend and apply with the prod environment:

```bash
terraform -chdir=infra init -reconfigure -backend-config=backend/prod.hcl
terraform -chdir=infra apply -var="env=prod"
```

### 8. Check the live URL

{{> aws/live-check urlCommand="terraform -chdir=infra output -raw api_url"}}

`output` reads the state of the backend initialized last, so run it right after the `apply` of the environment you want to check.

### 9. Deploy from GitHub Actions

On a push to `main` the workflow deploys `dev`; a manual run deploys `dev` or `prod`. The GitHub environments are named after the Terraform environments.

{{> aws/github-oidc environments="dev prod"}}
